## Runtime & Modules
- ESM only (`"type": "module"`). Use `import`/`export`; no `require`.
- Targets Node.js and Cloudflare Workers. Guard Node-only APIs from worker paths.

## Commands
**Dev**: `npm run dev` (Workers) | `npm run dev:node` (Node)
**Build**: `npm run build` | `npm run build-plugins`
**Test**: `npm run test:gateway` | `npm run test:plugins`
**Deploy**: `npm run deploy` (Workers) | `npm run start:node` (Node prod)

## Architecture
**Entrypoints**
- `src/index.ts` — Cloudflare Workers entry
- `src/start-server.ts` — Node.js HTTP server entry

**Core Paths**
- `src/handlers/**` — Route logic (validate early, return typed results)
- `src/middlewares/**` — Cross-cutting concerns (auth, cache, logging, guardrails)
- `src/services/**` — Orchestration and provider composition
- `src/providers/**` — AI provider adapters (normalize to internal types)
- `src/types/**` — Shared type definitions
- `src/utils/**` — Pure utility functions
- `plugins/**` — Guardrail and validation plugins

**Dependency Flow**: handlers → services → providers (avoid circular deps)

